{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790285935,"nonce":"MGNlve/RRiNZhj3RyBUO78YGh3E=","title":"CI Windows: zyntax_python's build script overflows the main thread's stack","message":"The Windows native-tests job has failed since run 35537352465 (2026-09-20) with `failed to run custom build command for zyntax_python ... exit code: 0xc00000fd, STATUS_STACK_OVERFLOW` (\"thread 'main' has overflowed its stack\"). The build script lowers the whole shared library to a snapshot on the main thread, which Windows gives 1 MB (Linux and macOS give 8 MB).\n\nReproduced on macOS by running the debug build script under `ulimit -s 1024`: zyntax_python and zyntax_lua both abort with a stack overflow; both pass at 2 MB and up. zynml's build script (grammar and stdlib parse) passes at 256 KB and fails at 128 KB, so it has less headroom than Windows' x86_64 debug frames may allow.\n\nFix: each of the three build scripts runs its work on a spawned thread with a 256 MB stack and joins it, propagating the error and any panic. After the fix all three pass with the main thread at 128 KB.","files":null}]}